      "method": "chronos2",
      "location": "src/marine_echo/training/native_chronos.py:121-221; tools/execute_native_chronos.py:38-43",
      "finding": "The advertised complete two-hour slot is not enforced. The internal timer starts after corpus loading and context preparation, checks the deadline only after each shard, and excludes final concatenation, prediction-artifact saving, scoring and result saving. Model loading or a single inference call can exceed the deadline before control reaches a check. Resume accounting also omits preparation and work after the last saved manifest. The ownership wrapper has no independent deadline watchdog.",
      "required_change": "Use a separately bound owned-child supervisor covering startup, loading, preparation, inference, evaluation, saving and failed/resumed attempts. Enforce the remaining cumulative two-hour comparator allowance and remaining aggregate 96-hour programme allowance, journal actual owned walltime and exit, and terminate only its owned child. The existing execute_native_ssl_job.py hardcodes the neural runner and does not supervise this Chronos wrapper."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "severity": "BLOCKING",
      "method": "chronos2",
      "location": "tools/execute_native_chronos.py:38-40; src/marine_echo/training/native_chronos.py:183-188",
      "finding": "The wrapper calls Resources.snapshot only after run returns. Consequently its reported peak_rss_bytes is effectively a completion sample. Chronos samples current RSS between shards, which can miss loading or prediction peaks and does not update the Resources peak-RSS accumulator. The retained allocator fraction and CUDA maximum-memory checks do not establish the separate process-RAM limit.",
      "required_change": "Include continuous owned-process RSS monitoring and honest peak reporting in the comparator supervisor requested by C1. Cover loading and long inference calls, not only shard boundaries."
    },
